{
  "_comment": [
    "Mixed-age Terraform state record for issue #5831. See README.md in this",
    "directory for provenance and for what each field is doing here.",
    "",
    "Two resource records of DIFFERENT ages, which is the whole point:",
    "  aws_eks_addon.coredns      — written by a NEWER provider: carries",
    "                               namespace_config and the four identity",
    "                               fields that provider 5.x cannot serialise.",
    "  aws_launch_template.gvisor_nodes — written by an OLDER provider:",
    "                               schema_version 0, while provider 6.16.0+",
    "                               declares schema version 1.",
    "",
    "A fixture carrying only the first record passes on the raised provider",
    "floor while the real targeted plan still fails. That happened on this",
    "issue. Both ages must be present or the test certifies the wrong thing.",
    "",
    "Terraform ignores unknown top-level keys, so this comment is inert.",
    "It is a literal string array, not a real state field."
  ],

